\subsection{Putting it all together}

% \frank{our indices are a bit off in this subsection I think; earlier we used that we had $\log_{1+eps} (2\Delta) -1$ levels here we only use $\log_{1+eps} \Delta$.}
% \frank{I'm guessing \opt in this section again refers to the weight of the EMST of the points no? However, in Lemma~\ref{lem:reduction} \opt denotes the optimal cost of the MST in the spanner $S$. So I think that in the proof of the Lemma~\ref{lem:emst_proof} below we still need to readjust the choice of $\eps$ to account for this no? I.e. I guess we want to apply Lemma~\ref{lem:reduction} with $\eps = \eps/2$ or so. 
