No stable sequence can offer both agents a per-round average utility of $1$. Then, for the agent who does not receive a per-round average utility of $1$, they are incentivized to deviate on the first action in which they do not receive utility $1$ (then receiving utility $1$). Hence, rock-paper-scissors has no stable sequences.    
