\section{Synthetic Data Generation}
% \subsection{Synthetic Data Generation}
Our study aims to analyze the impact of language composition on CLIR performance. As recent embedding models utilize a diverse range of datasets, employing open-source data might risk overlapping with previously-trained data.
To address this potential contamination issue and more robustly assess the effect of language composition, we build a high-quality, diverse training dataset, utilizing GPT-4o~\cite{openai_api} for the entire generation process.
\paragraph{KDC Sampling}
To ensure broad domain coverage and overcome potential LLM domain limitations, we incorporate the Korean Decimal Classification (KDC)~\citep{oh2020korean}. KDC is a Korean adaptation of the Dewey Decimal Classification (DDC)~\citep{scott1998dewey}, a comprehensive library classification system. KDC has a hierarchical structure, where each digit represents a specific subject level: the first digit signifies a broad subject area, the second a more specific category, and the third a subcategory. We systematically sample categories across various hierarchical levels of KDC, from broad subject areas down to specific subcategories.
% , to ensure comprehensive topic representation in our synthesized data. 
% . KDC has a hierarchical structure, where each digit represents a specific subject level: the first digit signifies a broad subject area, the second a more specific category, and the third a subcategory.
\paragraph{Task Brainstorming \& Triple Generation}
Adapting methods from previous study~\cite{E5_Mistral}, task descriptions are first brainstormed for each sampled KDC category. These descriptions then serve as prompts for generating \{query, positive, hard\_negative\} triples (see Appendix~\ref{appen:prompt_example} for prompt examples). To enhance training effectiveness, we mine 6 hard negatives for each query (detailed in Appendix~\ref{appen_hn_mining}) and subsequently generate 8 distinct Korean-English language combination datasets to cover all linguistic permutations.
