is defined if and only if
$\Var(E) \subseteq \Dom(\sigma) $. Similarly, for boolean  and distribution expressions, $\Sem{B}_\sigma$ and
$\Sem{D}_\sigma$
are defined
if and only 
$\Var(B) \subseteq \Dom(\sigma)$ and $ \Var(D) \subseteq \Dom(\sigma)$ respectively. When defined, we have  $\Sem{E}_\sigma \in \Int$, 
$\,\Sem{B}_\sigma \in \{\True,\False\}$ (our notation for truth values) and $\Sem{D}_\sigma \in \Dist(\Int)$.
