\section{CONCLUSION}
This paper introduced \textbf{CAF-I}, an LLM-driven multi-agent framework for robust irony detection, integrating specialized context, semantic, and rhetoric agents with collaborative refinement. Experiments confirmed CAF-I's state-of-the-art zero-shot performance over existing methods. Ablation studies validated its component necessity and architectural robustness, while also highlighting its interpretability and error correction.

