    \item $\{v_i\} \in K$ for every $v_i \in [v_n]$.
\end{enumerate}


Or, for any number $k$ the $k$ simplex is made out of $k+1$ vertices, is $k-1$ dimensional. 
Algebraic topology allows us to manipulate these simplicial complexes, and observe in higher dimensional spaces. \\ 
