    \item \textbf{Filtration Step 1} (\( \epsilon = 0 \)): Points are isolated: \( \beta_0 = 4 \), \( \beta_1 = 0 \).
    \item \textbf{Filtration Step 2} (\( \epsilon > 0 \)): Edges appear, merging points: \( \beta_0 = 2 \), \( \beta_1 = 0 \).
    \item \textbf{Filtration Step 3} (\( \epsilon > 0.5 \)): Loops form: \( \beta_0 = 1 \), \( \beta_1 = 1 \).
    \item \textbf{Filtration Step 4} (\( \epsilon \) large): Loops close and fill in triangles: \( \beta_0 = 1 \), \( \beta_1 = 0 \).
\end{itemize}
The barcode representation tracks the persistence of features:

\[
\begin{array}{|c|c|}
\hline
\textbf{Feature (Dimension)} & \textbf{Barcode (Birth - Death)} \\
\hline
\text{Connected Components (\( \beta_0 \))} & [0, 0.5], [0, 0.5], [0, 1.0], [0, \infty] \\
\hline
\text{Loops (\( \beta_1 \))} & [0.5, 1.5] \\
\hline
\end{array}
\]

