\end{figure}

The OPT-125M model's moral scores for the PEW dataset, as illustrated in  Figure~\ref{fig10}, generally show smaller variations across most topics compared to the GPT-2 base model, with the notable exception of 'gambling,' which displays significant spread. Additionally, like the GPT-2, the scores are predominantly shifted towards the positive side, suggesting a more favorable moral assessment of most topics.

\begin{figure}[ht]
