(b) The same plot with a directional cue (red arrow), underscoring how the agent’s hidden states transition smoothly along the ring as it moves through the environment. The circular shape suggests robust encoding of continuous spatial factors, reflecting an internally consistent strategy rather than rote stimulus-response mappings.}
